# Bashan OS — answer the one firmware licence question in advance.
#
# firmware-ipw2x00 asks, in its PRE-INSTALL script, whether you accept
# Intel's licence. In a build chroot there is no one to ask, so the script
# exits with "agree question could not be asked", dpkg aborts, and the whole
# build fails. That is what killed the second Part G build.
#
# It is the ONLY package we ship that does this - checked by unpacking the
# maintainer scripts of all 21 firmware packages in the list and grepping
# for a licence prompt.
#
# NOTE FOR THE LAWYER: pre-answering this means Bashan Tech LLC accepts
# Intel's firmware licence on behalf of every user, silently. Debian's own
# installer asks the user once instead. Recorded in
# docs/legal/BLOCKS-PUBLIC-RELEASE.md.
firmware-ipw2x00 firmware-ipw2x00/license/accepted boolean true
